  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A body weight <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi></math>, is projected vertically upwards from earth&#39;s surface to reach a height above the earth which is equal to nine times the radius of earth. The weight of the body at that height will be:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "zdzoZ",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mn>91</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Y79tV",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "8M1Qv",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "YNgRQ",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/7bc09ec3-0c9a-49b0-9215-01afb7d39e55-9895973.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 201px;\" /></p><p>Final distance from the centre of earth wil be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>R</mi></math>.</p><p>Now acceleration due to gravity at any height(distance from centre r) is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>10</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p>Now, value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi></math>&nbsp;at surface will be,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>M</mi></mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Hence,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math>.</p><p>Then,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
